[{"id":"VRCE-3-47-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing those words of Sītā the highly powerful Ten necked one striking his hands together, increased his body too high.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d8949123f0e39700f95d87c275dea2df7b737469cd5394c363f1ce228de5f9b6","compact":"bcbaaf6598f1b7c55a021633806f68d944b6614e735e505036b15f4970c280af","nasal":"bcbaaf6598f1b7c55a021633806f68d944b6614e735e505036b15f4970c280af"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":2,"english":"Thereupon, that one skilled in speech again spake to Maithili, Methinks you have run mad. Have you not heard of my valour and prowess?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.613,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"98334ff0baad8574dcfa93d31bc2fa83c6ea02b27c2644ea65ecc5a41231e7e0","compact":"4fcb2e33ce7e90f0507eda70adb4265046e929de32c979808901c9f68f03bba1","nasal":"4fcb2e33ce7e90f0507eda70adb4265046e929de32c979808901c9f68f03bba1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":3,"english":"Stationing myself in the welkin I can with my hands raise up the earth. I can drink up the waters of the ocean. And engaged in conflict I can destroy Death itself","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5217e874bddc38fbea6858b355945942736090219f6671438d68087640e1daa7","compact":"4e7ff6250e2cd2a5cfee18e4b5ee09ff12b85a308d1a50a7d853c54c30052d1d","nasal":"ca2b9b7c557a1c6b867059f9ca716a9f4978ae784c7ff22d26728fbf3fc8ec18"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":4,"english":"With my sharpened shafts I can pierce the Sun and cut asunder the earth. You are mad with your beauty. Do you look upon me, who am capable of illusions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.658,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"14e410a5a4136288a01e06f63c54032fb0cc885822b24b99d30adbce4af16b19","compact":"59b45d29cc5f06c811754e6ec34dbd2ab595437c229d432cbae470404557088e","nasal":"342b7c7422eb0dabc70e69cd61393964915b6d4c5aafe6f860609832509f0eb7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":5,"english":"When he had spoken thus, his yellow eyes became blood-red with rage and assumed the, semblance of flaming fire.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cc9b5dcf8cfa4f9bff36c54cdc6f578dc8dd4e33758d851aa0e684a5b61e1062","compact":"ff7273bdc616b19af9fe34f592508a3c01209a243b104c4ea5a5a8460c6aacab","nasal":"dd5a55771a90b972d3e20d838c2fa979e8ac2c308e1eb87547dfc7177705a8ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":6,"english":"Thereat Răvana, the younger brother of the Lord of wealth, changing his placid countenance, instantly assumed his own terrible shape resembling that of Yama.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.79,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a60ec742577445b127077ce9795b49a17e5c505ca178d241d1163e15fdfcce4a","compact":"e24bdabeaa355bbbce000274889bf658044a4202cef2ede40cdb3cf4780b325d","nasal":"e24bdabeaa355bbbce000274889bf658044a4202cef2ede40cdb3cf4780b325d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":7,"english":"Highly exercised with ire, that ranger of the night became of ten countenances and twenty arms; his eyes were bloody and he appeared beautiful like to blue clouds, being dressed in gold-hued apparel.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.459,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f887e167e4c8f12bec706841914b833163fde369a345164deee594d7080e9a47","compact":"b2eac0d9eb0503d76a3c67485de92f0434304a35db782becf71417d5226179c4","nasal":"91f3eb12801ca53b58273f16b8ed7219da6ea86053ffb6356eda97307ce5294d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":8,"english":"Highly exercised with ire, that ranger of the night became of ten countenances and twenty arms; his eyes were bloody and he appeared beautiful like to blue clouds, being dressed in gold-hued apparel. Leaving aside the semblance of a mendicant, that lord of Raksasas, Ravana, increasing in bulk, assumed his own shape. And wearing a blood-red cloth he stood there fixing his look upon that jewel of a damsel–Maithili.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.466,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-7","DUTT-3-49-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3001900acf9c18006e927471ce92393b4a369a6086bf7546a3c5e768880f0259","compact":"0a27c097ee0b1c80543730a4f6b85581c5f71546804ad89c4e2e77e2b0201fd3","nasal":"0a27c097ee0b1c80543730a4f6b85581c5f71546804ad89c4e2e77e2b0201fd3"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":9,"english":"Leaving aside the semblance of a mendicant, that lord of Raksasas, Ravana, increasing in bulk, assumed his own shape. And wearing a blood-red cloth he stood there fixing his look upon that jewel of a damsel–Maithili.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.563,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4445bec767937772230457b749bf78c133036c89a8f547074dad204db6b90c8d","compact":"8d59be73f317572f60000a9f366efa710a1ed493784d407f589ea18b2a6a421e","nasal":"28b6776596a42034b6a580af398bdf3e491ca6e73d5db89f90122ffd8e03e8c1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":10,"english":"Thereupon Rāvaņa spake to Mathili like to the rays of the sun, having a head of black hair and wearing apparel and ornaments, saying, O you fine damsel, if you did wish to have a husband known all over the world, do you surrender yourself to me.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"25bf4c3c00b007cca930a1e470a228c93473b97549060ae3c5bc8d398ca1d222","compact":"b1999c83791720106b320d5b5a8155ac793e121cd76602d1f1de428d10bbfb7c","nasal":"d3d3aa63c5b11fa9b805c5de61ca5bb73e6e4f8d12747064fa7dc054f9f46516"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":11,"english":"Thereupon Rāvaņa spake to Mathili like to the rays of the sun, having a head of black hair and wearing apparel and ornaments, saying, O you fine damsel, if you did wish to have a husband known all over the world, do you surrender yourself to me.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.741,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f32c5d2ae28cca02645f2229f9d70e5975d8156c76ce291f11eb65c57e6e2393","compact":"12202c7c725cb502d03f7b9a876e6f505f0b1898e620b5399c69fb999d92c69f","nasal":"12202c7c725cb502d03f7b9a876e6f505f0b1898e620b5399c69fb999d92c69f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":12,"english":"I am a worthy husband for you. Do you serve me for ever, your praiseworthy husband. O fine lady, I hall never do what you did not like.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.48,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e5f003506932f6b7a17e3677444a2bba28a7da7ff79ea0ceedb3a3db95047e3","compact":"49990c07eb23a81d77e54a58abadca7945fc9f6aca803df4047037128d1d967b","nasal":"49990c07eb23a81d77e54a58abadca7945fc9f6aca803df4047037128d1d967b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":13,"english":"Renouncing your attachment for a man, do you place your love in me. O foolish girl, worthy of being adored by the learned, for what quality are you attached to Rāma of a limited life, who has been deprived of his kingdom and has his desire frustrated, and who of an evil intent, has, at the words of his wife, renouncing his kingdom and kinsmen, been living in this forest-the abode of voracious animals.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"06d18cd8e778756ee0055fa23ade73530414bfeb683155db1a9a8f3ec8c098a8","compact":"5e6a687