"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d0226c26c7e7206d14bec031029d2645037545d972d66c5d2805667aaae3499","compact":"cc256da3755dd2c42fe6411a3b779447088aa3822e4cdce483d2d6414f48701a","nasal":"cc256da3755dd2c42fe6411a3b779447088aa3822e4cdce483d2d6414f48701a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-25","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":25,"english":"O you the subduer of foes, you did always control the rebellious,-why do you not punish such a vicious Rākşasa?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047025","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6e5527de2eecbb65d3e22d07ad74bb8101a17ef2e6dc2302ffb624cd1a9c31f1","compact":"ae92c443b6707e9932acfae857c7b5d85ef1165c3f90cd17b80c0df05c9ffa29","nasal":"ae92c443b6707e9932acfae857c7b5d85ef1165c3f90cd17b80c0df05c9ffa29"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-26","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":26,"english":"The vicious do not instantaneously meet with the fruits of their actions, as for corn to ripen requires the assistance of time.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-49-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3047026","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c284e647f40eeedb5d59091442579cdcef874f74e19f9a3f82edb39d0373eb5","compact":"6f67a6570644b45c02188a0fd84c13c4cae6e8bdde9a9cc5e7a965dda4bf6ea1","nasal":"6db293deca6add7cf9d9c2ef5160c53853452301e0f470a6ad87c954b756535e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-47-27","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":47,"verse":27,"english":"For this iniquitous deed, which you have perpetrated, availing of the time and losing your sense, you shall meet with a mighty disaster from Rāma, bringing about your end.","alignme